  },
  "bugs": {
   "url": "https://github.com/AgentDeskAI/browser-tools-mcp/issues"
  },
  "description": "MCP server exposing live browser telemetry (console logs, network requests, screenshots, Lighthouse audits) from your real Chrome session",
  "dist-tags": {
   "latest": "2.0.2"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/AgentDeskAI/browser-tools-mcp#readme",
  "keywords": [
   "mcp",
   "model-context-protocol",
   "browser",
   "tools",
   "debugging",
   "ai",
   "chrome",
   "extension",
   "lighthouse",
   "telemetry"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "maintainers": [
   {
    "email": "[redacted-email:f8f9878f48f9]",
    "name": "tedjames24"
   }
  ],
  "name": "@agentdeskai/browser-tools-mcp",
  "readme": "# @agentdeskai/browser-tools-mcp\n\nMCP server exposing live browser telemetry \u2014 console output, network requests,\nscreenshots and Lighthouse audits \u2014 from your real Chrome session.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"browser-tools\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@agentdeskai/browser-tools-mcp@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis package embeds the browser connector, so it is the only process you need to\nrun. Pair it with the Chrome extension from the\n[repository](https://github.com/AgentDeskAI/browser-tools-mcp).\n\nRequires Node 22.19 or newer. Run with `--doctor` to check your setup, or\n`--help` for all options.\n\nFull documentation, tool reference and security notes:\nhttps://github.com/AgentDeskAI/browser-tools-mcp\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
  "repository": {
   "directory": "browser-tools-mcp",
   "type": "git",
   "url": "git+https://github.com/AgentDeskAI/browser-tools-mcp.git"
  },
